WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.072
Welcome to Grade 4 English, Unit 8:
Tools, Machines, and Everyday Items.

2
00:00:05.152 --> 00:00:12.370
This unit is all about the tools, machines, and
everyday items we use at home, at school, and at work.

3
00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:20.456
You will learn the names of many useful objects — from a
stapler and a microwave to a telescope and a helicopter.

4
00:00:20.536 --> 00:00:27.826
You will also learn how to describe what these things
do, how to give safe instructions for using them,

5
00:00:27.906 --> 00:00:31.332
and how to talk about working together as a crew.

6
00:00:31.412 --> 00:00:38.774
By the end of the unit, you will be ready to read
and enjoy this unit's mystery story, “The Attic Clue”,

7
00:00:38.854 --> 00:00:46.001
about a class in Rwanda who discover old tools in
a dusty attic and build something amazing together.

8
00:00:46.081 --> 00:00:52.011
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

9
00:00:52.091 --> 00:01:00.477
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name and
describe many tools, machines, and everyday items in English.

10
00:01:00.557 --> 00:01:07.617
You will also describe an object using adjectives
and a relative clause with who, that, or which.

11
00:01:07.697 --> 00:01:13.801
You will also say what people have to do
to stay safe when using tools and machines.

12
00:01:13.881 --> 00:01:16.525
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:01:16.605 --> 00:01:22.401
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
equipment, folder, briefcase, shield, stapler, hardware.

14
00:01:22.481 --> 00:01:27.067
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:27.147 --> 00:01:30.697
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:30.777 --> 00:01:35.709
The reading sequence includes The Right
Tool for the Job and A Look at the Stars.

17
00:01:35.789 --> 00:01:36.576
Read actively.

18
00:01:36.656 --> 00:01:40.846
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:40.926 --> 00:01:44.868
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:44.948 --> 00:01:49.681
The first language focus is Defining
Relative Clauses (who, that, which).

21
00:01:49.761 --> 00:01:56.932
A defining relative clause is an extra part of a sentence
that tells us exactly which person or thing we mean.

22
00:01:57.012 --> 00:02:03.525
For example, in “the tool that joins papers,” the
words “that joins papers” tell us it is a stapler.

23
00:02:03.605 --> 00:02:07.942
This helps us describe the tools
and machines in this unit clearly.

24
00:02:08.022 --> 00:02:15.127
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

25
00:02:15.207 --> 00:02:19.312
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Describe an Everyday Item.

26
00:02:19.392 --> 00:02:23.375
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

27
00:02:23.455 --> 00:02:26.468
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

28
00:02:26.548 --> 00:02:29.682
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

29
00:02:29.762 --> 00:02:31.208
You are ready to begin.

30
00:02:31.288 --> 00:02:37.773
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

31
00:02:37.853 --> 00:02:40.956
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

32
00:02:41.036 --> 00:02:48.450
Use the AI tutor for hints and feedback any time, and
bring your questions to a live session too if you join one.
